# Texture-path containment fixture (deep audit 2026-09, finding F2).
#
# A model names its own textures, and those names are FILE CONTENT. This quad
# names two of them OUTSIDE its own directory, which is legal in every mesh
# format and is exactly the shape of the finding: before containment landed,
# both were resolved verbatim, opened, hashed into the content-addressed store
# as "textures" of this asset, and written into every export of the project.
#
# The suite (tests/importer/test_importer_security.cpp) copies this directory
# to <tmp>/outer/inner/model/ and plants a readable "secret" at
# <tmp>/outer/outside_secret.png, which is precisely where ../../ points.
#
#   escapes_no_fallback     ../../outside_secret.png — nothing of that name
#                           sits beside the model, so the reference must be
#                           DROPPED (and warned about).
#   escapes_with_fallback   ../../beside.png — beside.png DOES sit beside the
#                           model (the suite writes it), so containment falls
#                           back to that copy: the innocent real-world case is
#                           a DCC tool writing an authoring-machine path for a
#                           texture that ships with the model.
mtllib traversal.mtl

v 0.0 0.0 0.0
v 1.0 0.0 0.0
v 0.0 1.0 0.0
v 1.0 1.0 0.0

vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 0.0 1.0
vt 1.0 1.0

vn 0.0 0.0 1.0

usemtl escapes_no_fallback
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1

usemtl escapes_with_fallback
f 2/2/1 4/4/1 3/3/1
